# Environment files.
#
# There are none in this project today, but the presence function is exactly the
# sort of thing someone adds a token to later, and a committed .env is the one
# mistake that cannot be undone by rotating it. `.env.example` is exempt so the
# shape of a needed variable can still be committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

